cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite this software artifact."
type: software
title: "Lean certificates for analytic obstructions and local phase survival"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
authors:
  - name: "humanaiconvention"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/humanaiconvention/rh"
url: "https://github.com/humanaiconvention/rh/tree/main/qrh-obstructions-lean"
abstract: >-
  Complete Lean 4 proofs of three obstructions to an unchanged one-half
  substitution in a specified analytic architecture: Euler-defect
  non-summability over Eisenstein prime ideals, an exact 3/8 exponent
  deficit, and a moment-parameter mismatch; also a local conjugate-slot
  phase polynomial and nonvanishing certificate at norm 157. The artifact
  concerns the explicit local factor, supplied parameters, and stated
  phase relations. It does not certify the source analytic estimates,
  native Gauss-sum identification, or regularization operation, or exclude
  alternative continuation methods.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Euler products
  - prime ideals
  - reproducible mathematics
